Subject: [PATCH] dt510: propagate STOP failures and clear the I2C bus

Build 691 times out waiting for STOP after the LT9611 crystal-clock
selection, reports that transfer as successful, then loses arbitration
and address ACK on the next page-selection transaction.

Retain STOP errors from write, PIO-read and DMA-read completion. Disable
the controller before one standard bus-recovery attempt, and preserve
the original transfer errno. Do not replay arbitrary client messages.
Never invoke sleepable GPIO recovery from the atomic transfer path.

Permit the LT9611's idempotent initialization sequence to retry timeout
as well as arbitration loss within its existing three-attempt budget.
DT510 separately supplies recovery pinctrl and GPIOs in its device tree.
This is a bounded recovery candidate, not proof of crystal readiness.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [DT510 bring-up candidate against NXP kernel]
Assisted-by: Briar
---
--- a/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-imx.c
+++ b/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-imx.c
@@ -263,6 +263,7 @@
 	unsigned long		i2csr;
